---
// The about text, shared by the About dialog on the homepage and the /about/ page, so
// the two can't drift apart.
---

<div class="columns">
  <p>
    I'm Roger Egito, a game designer and Unity developer from Brazil. These days I design
    games at Ludomancer Studio and lead a VR project at UFF's Media Lab.
    <br /><br />
    I approach every project with deep care and a drive to deliver work that's both
    functional and thoughtful. I always look to understand the purpose behind the
    project and deliver something I'm proud to stand behind.
  </p>
  <p>
    I like building games that have meaning, fun mechanics, tell stories, and engage
    people. I consider games to be an art medium that can genuinely help people.
    <br /><br />
    Whether I'm designing gameplay mechanics, creating immersive interfaces, writing
    narratives or developing backend solutions, I enjoy the process and I'm always
    willing to give it my all.
  </p>
  <p>
    When I'm not programming or designing games, I enjoy playing video games, watching
    anime, GM'ing RPGs and spending time with family and friends.
    <br /><br />
    If you're looking for a developer who genuinely cares about the product and is
    ready to bring strong technical skills, creative problem-solving, and a
    user-centered mindset to your team, let's talk.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  /* Three columns on a wide screen, stacked on a narrow one. */
  .columns {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-gap);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-gap);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .columns p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
